<title>TURKEY: Turkey 5th beet test shows 4.87 T sugar per ha.</title>
<headline>Turkey 5th beet test shows 4.87 T sugar per ha.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Turkey's fifth beet test, carried out on August 15, showed a rise to 4.87 tonnes of sugar per hectare from 4.67 tonnes at the same point in 1995, Turkey's state sugar refineries Turkseker said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said average sugar content was 14.0 percent, unchanged from the previous year's corresponding test.</p>
<p>Turkey holds beet tests at 15-day intervals. Data for the fifth test came from 28 refineries throughout the country.</p>
<p>Details follow.</p>
<p>			     5th test 96    5th test 95    4th test 96</p>
<p>Sugar weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)     4.870	    4.670	    3.510</p>
<p>Average sugar</p>
<p> content (pct)	     14.0	     14.0	     13.0</p>
<p>Number of beets</p>
<p> per hectare		 78,600	   82,580	   78,580</p>
<p>Root weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)    34.800	   33.460	   26.820</p>
<p>Ratio of leaf</p>
<p>weight to beet weight</p>
<p> (leaf/beet)		  0.76	     0.81	     1.01</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
